# What must NOT ride to Vercel.
#
# The first production deploy uploaded 202 MB for a 34 MB site: the working
# tree carries a quarantine of retired renders, the raw Drive drop, a previous
# dist/ and the PSDs the finishes were cut from. None of it is served — the
# build runs `python3 build.py`, which writes dist/ from assets/ — so all of it
# was upload time and storage spent on nothing.
#
# Keep this in step with build.py: anything build.py does not read, and the
# site does not serve, belongs here.

_quarantine/
_drive/
_dev/
dist/

# generated locally by the build; Vercel builds its own
*.bak-*
*.psd
*.rar
*.zip

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# the tools are how the assets were made, not part of the site
tools_*.py

# The PNG masters: 170 MB of the 202 MB first upload, and build.py already
# skips every one of them (only the WebP copies ship). They are the source the
# finishes are cut from, and that work happens on this machine, not on Vercel.
assets/products/*.png
assets/products/face/*.png
assets/products/thumb/*.png
